    32	# Getting Started
    33	
    34	## Requirements
    35	Before getting started, ensure that your machine meets the specifications outlined in the [Requirements](REQUIREMENTS.md) file.
    36	## Setup
    37	Additionally, please refer to the [Installation Guide](INSTALL.md) for detailed instructions on setting up the necessary environment to run our experiments.
    38	
    39	
    40	# Dataset Description
    41	The dataset of the artifact exists in the `data/` directory and has the following structure:
    42	```
    43	├── data
    44	│   ├── results
    45	│   │   ├── rq1a.csv
    46	│   │   ├── rq1b.csv
    47	│   │   ├── rq2a.csv
    48	│   │   └── rq2b.csv
    49	│   │   ├── qualitative_results.json
    50	│   ├── project_dependencies_post_data_collection.json
    51	│   ├── project_dependencies_final.json
    52	│   ├── security
    53	│   │   ├── project_vulnerabilities.json
    54	│   │   ├── pypi_vulnerabilities.csv
    55	│   │   ├── vulnerability2function.json
    56	│   │   └── vulnerable_dependencies.json
    57	│   └── subset
    58	│       ├── sample_projects.csv
    59	```
    60	Bellow, we describe the contents of each file:
    61	
    62	- `results/`: This directory stores the bre-baked dataset of the automated and manual analysis performed in order to produce the results (numbers, figures, tables) reported on the results section of our paper (Sections 3.1-3.4)
    63	  - `rq1a.csv`: Contains the quantitative analysis results for the first research question (RQ1), focusing especially on the prevalence of bloat at different granularities in the Python projects.
    64	    - Columns:
    65	      - `project`: GitHub Owner-Repository Name.
    66	      - `NBD`: Number of Bloated Dependencies – Represents the number of bloated dependencies identified in the project.
    67	      - `NBFD`: Number of Bloated Files in Dependencies – Measures the count of bloated files identified within the dependencies of the project.
    68	      - `NBMD`: Number of Bloated Methods in Dependencies – Indicates the count of bloated methods found within the dependencies of the project.
    69	      - `NBD-LOC`: Number of Bloated Dependencies in LOC - Denotes the lines of code (LOC) in the bloated dependencies.
    70	      - `NBFD-LOC`: Number of Bloated Files in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the lines of code (LOC) in the bloated files of the dependencies.
    71	      - `NBMD-LOC`: Number of Bloated Methods in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the number of lines of code (LOC) in the bloated methods of the dependencies.
    72	      - `PBD`: Percentage of Bloated Dependencies – Represents the proportion of dependencies that are identified as bloated in the project.
    73	      - `PBFD`: Percentage of Bloated Files in Dependencies – Represents the proportion of files within the dependencies that are identified as bloated.
    74	      - `PBMD`: Percentage of Bloated Methods in Dependencies – Represents the proportion of methods within the dependencies of the project that are identified as bloated.
    75	      - `PBD-LOC`: Percentage of Bloated Dependencies in LOC - Represents the percentage of lines of code (LOC) in dependencies that are bloated
    76	      - `PBFD-LOC`: Percentage of Bloated Files in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the percentage of lines of code (LOC) in dependency files that are bloated.
    77	      - `PBMD-LOC`: Percentage of Bloated Methods in Dependencies in LOC - Represents the percentage of lines of code (LOC) in dependency methods that are bloated.
    78	      - `unique_unresolved_count`: The number of unique unresolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    79	      - `unique_resolved_count`: The number of unique resolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    80	      - `unresolved_count`: The total number of unresolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    81	      - `resolved_count`: The total number of resolved external calls during the Stitching process.
    82	
    83	- `rq1b.csv`: For each Python project, this file includes the different usage statuses of its direct and transitive dependencies, showcasing metrics related to bloat and usage in various granularities (RQ1).
    84	  - Columns:
    85	    - `product`: GitHub Owner-Repository Name.
    86	    - `bloated_deps_count_1`: Number of bloated direct dependencies.
    87	    - `bloated_deps_loc_1`: Lines of code in bloated direct dependencies.
    88	    - `bloated_files_count_1`: Number of bloated files in direct dependencies.
    89	    - `bloated_files_loc_1`: Lines of code in the bloated files of direct dependencies.
    90	    - `bloated_functions_count_1`: Number of bloated functions in direct dependencies.
    91	    - `bloated_functions_loc_1`: Total number of lines of code in the bloated functions of direct dependencies.
    92	    - `used_direct_deps_count_1`: Number of used direct dependencies.
    93	    - `used_direct_deps_count_1`: Lines of code in used direct dependencies.
    94	    - `used_direct_files_count_1`: Number of used files in direct dependencies.
    95	    - `used_direct_files_loc_1`: Lines of code in the used files of direct dependencies.
    96	    - `used_direct_functions_count_1`: Number of used functions in direct dependencies.
    97	    - `used_direct_functions_loc_1`: Lines of code in the used functions of direct dependencies.
    98	    - `transitive_bloated_dependencies_count`: Number of bloated transitive dependencies.
    99	    - `transitive_bloated_dependencies_loc`: Lines of code in bloated transitive dependencies.
